  "id": "COMPOUND:40778 - PROTEIN:6346",
  "verbalization": "Mollicelline K is implicated in the regulation of the DNMT3A2/3L complex through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicelline K acts as a target of several compounds, which in turn target the DNMT3A2/3L complex. Specifically, it is linked to fusion glycoprotein F0, which is targeted by cis-Isopinocamphone, and to asialoglycoprotein receptor 2, which is targeted by 3-Hydroxymollugin. These intermediates ultimately lead to the DNMT3A2/3L complex. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some evidence pointing to different intermediates that ultimately converge on the DNMT3A2/3L complex. The integration of these pathways suggests that Mollicelline K may modulate the activity of the DNMT3A2/3L complex through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
